# Go standard library / x/net findings in /usr/bin/caddy of the base image
# caddy:alpine (built with Go 1.26.8, fixed in 1.26.10). Not fixable here
# without building Caddy ourselves; every rebuild pulls the then-current
# caddy:alpine, so delete these lines as soon as the scan passes without them.
# Exposure: Caddy listens on :8080 inside the pod and only the pod's
# oauth2-proxy talks to it (NetworkPolicy: the ingress controller reaches
# :4180 only); it terminates no TLS and speaks no HTTP/2 to clients.
# Review by 2026-11-30.
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-111943
CVE-2026-97031

# go-jose/v4 v4.1.5 in /usr/bin/caddy of the base image caddy:alpine (new since 2026-10-27; fixed in
# go-jose 4.1.6). Checked 2026-10-29: Caddy 2.11.7 is the latest release and the current caddy:alpine still
# has 4.1.5, so there is no image to move to; the fix would be building Caddy ourselves (xcaddy), as for the
# findings above. Exposure: a DoS when a JWK with an RSA key is parsed; Caddy parses no JWKs from clients here,
# it only receives requests the pod's oauth2-proxy forwards on :8080 inside the pod.
# Delete as soon as the scan passes without it. Review by 2026-11-30.
CVE-2026-116587
